      mujiDigestEn: "Steppe pastoralists in Inner Mongolia perfected the collapsible felt dome yurt (Ger) engineered for gale resistance and seasonal migration. Throat singing (Khoomei), Long Song (Urtiin Duu), and the horsehead fiddle (Morin Khuur) are UNESCO-recognized sonic traditions.",
